# Design Doc Review (Step 1)

When the user says **"do a design doc review"** (or equivalent, e.g. "run a design doc review", "design doc review", "review the design doc"), treat it as a request to run the workflow in **`docs/prompts/01-design-doc-review.md`**.

1. **Read** `docs/prompts/01-design-doc-review.md` in full.
2. **Execute** the review exactly as specified in that prompt (workflow, review standard, finding requirements, output format, completion rule).
3. The design document to review is the one the user provides or the doc they have open (typically at `docs/in-progress/<feature>/<design-doc>.md`).

Do not substitute your own review process. Follow the prompt file’s instructions for passes, findings, edits, and final output. See `docs/prompts/README.md` for the full workflow (steps 1–5).
